	"data": "Play-Bleed\n\nThe path you take to a node is important context for the node itself.\n\nDefinition\n\nPlay-bleed is the property by which traversal history becomes a persistent characteristic of a node in a spatial knowledge graph. When you navigate to a node through a specific path, the experience of that traversal — how long you lingered, what you did there, where you came from — becomes part of the node's identity. The node is not objective. It is colored by the journey.\n\nThis is the fourth axis of…",
